{
  "name": "UK Legal Firm Client Portfolio",
  "description": "Comprehensive semantic model for analyzing UK law firm client relationships, case portfolios, financial performance, and solicitor workload",
  "compatibilityLevel": 1550,
  "model": {
    "culture": "en-GB",
    "tables": [
      {
        "name": "Cases",
        "description": "Fact table containing individual legal cases with financial and status information",
        "columns": [
          {
            "name": "case_id",
            "dataType": "string",
            "isHidden": false,
            "description": "Unique identifier for each legal case (e.g., CASE001, CASE002)"
          },
          {
            "name": "customer_id",
            "dataType": "string",
            "isHidden": false,
            "description": "Foreign key linking to Customers table"
          },
          {
            "name": "case_type",
            "dataType": "string",
            "isHidden": false,
            "description": "Type of legal case such as Conveyancing, Corporate Law, Family Law, Litigation. Synonyms: practice area, legal service type"
          },
          {
            "name": "case_value_gbp",
            "dataType": "int64",
            "isHidden": false,
            "summarizeBy": "none",
            "description": "Total financial value of the case in British Pounds. Synonyms: case worth, case revenue, billing amount, fee value"
          },
          {
            "name": "case_start_date",
            "dataType": "dateTime",
            "isHidden": false,
            "description": "Date when the case was opened and work began. This is the primary date field for time-based analysis."
          },
          {
            "name": "case_completion_date",
            "dataType": "dateTime",
            "isHidden": false,
            "description": "Date when the case was completed and closed. May be empty for ongoing cases. Synonyms: case closed date, completion date"
          },
          {
            "name": "assigned_solicitor_name",
            "dataType": "string",
            "isHidden": false,
            "description": "Name of the solicitor assigned to handle this case. Synonyms: lawyer name, attorney name, solicitor"
          },
          {
            "name": "high_value_case_flag",
            "dataType": "string",
            "isHidden": false,
            "description": "Indicates if this is a high-value case (Yes/No). High-value cases are defined as cases with value >= £50,000"
          },
          {
            "name": "payment_status",
            "dataType": "string",
            "isHidden": false,
            "description": "Current payment status of the case. Values: Paid (fully settled), Pending (awaiting payment), Overdue (past due date), Closed (case closed with payment settled). Synonyms: billing status, invoice status"
          }
        ],
        "measures": [
          {
            "name": "Total Case Value",
            "expression": "SUM(Cases[case_value_gbp])",
            "formatString": "\"£\"#,##0",
            "description": "Sum of all case values in British Pounds. Use this measure for total revenue, total billing, or total case portfolio value questions. Synonyms: total revenue, total fees, total billing"
          },
          {
            "name": "Average Case Value",
            "expression": "AVERAGE(Cases[case_value_gbp])",
            "formatString": "\"£\"#,##0",
            "description": "Average value per case in British Pounds. Use for analyzing typical case size or average billing per case. Synonyms: average fee, mean case value"
          },
          {
            "name": "Number of Cases",
            "expression": "COUNTROWS(Cases)",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "description": "Total count of legal cases. Use for case volume, caseload, or portfolio size questions. Synonyms: case count, number of matters, caseload"
          },
          {
            "name": "Number of Active Cases",
            "expression": "CALCULATE(COUNTROWS(Cases), Cases[payment_status] <> \"Closed\")",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "description": "Count of cases that are not yet closed (Pending, Paid, or Overdue status). Use for active caseload or ongoing work questions. Synonyms: active caseload, open cases, ongoing matters"
          },
          {
            "name": "Pending Payment Value",
            "expression": "CALCULATE(SUM(Cases[case_value_gbp]), Cases[payment_status] = \"Pending\")",
            "formatString": "\"£\"#,##0",
            "description": "Total value of cases with Pending payment status. Use for outstanding receivables or pending invoices questions. Synonyms: pending revenue, awaiting payment, outstanding fees"
          },
          {
            "name": "Overdue Payment Value",
            "expression": "CALCULATE(SUM(Cases[case_value_gbp]), Cases[payment_status] = \"Overdue\")",
            "formatString": "\"£\"#,##0",
            "description": "Total value of cases with Overdue payment status. Use for collections, late payments, or overdue invoices questions. Synonyms: overdue fees, late payments, collections"
          },
          {
            "name": "High Value Cases Count",
            "expression": "CALCULATE(COUNTROWS(Cases), Cases[high_value_case_flag] = \"Yes\")",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "description": "Count of high-value cases (cases >= £50,000). Use for strategic client or major matters questions"
          },
          {
            "name": "Case Completion Rate",
            "expression": "VAR CompletedCases = CALCULATE(COUNTROWS(Cases), NOT(ISBLANK(Cases[case_completion_date]))) VAR TotalCases = COUNTROWS(Cases) RETURN DIVIDE(CompletedCases, TotalCases, 0)",
            "formatString": "0.0%",
            "description": "Percentage of cases that have been completed (have a completion date). Use for productivity, efficiency, or throughput questions"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "Customers",
        "description": "Dimension table containing customer (client) demographic and contact information",
        "columns": [
          {
            "name": "customer_id",
            "dataType": "string",
            "isHidden": false,
            "description": "Unique identifier for each customer (e.g., C001, C002). Primary key. Synonyms: client ID"
          },
          {
            "name": "customer_name",
            "dataType": "string",
            "isHidden": false,
            "description": "Full name of the customer or company. Synonyms: client name, customer name"
          },
          {
            "name": "customer_type",
            "dataType": "string",
            "isHidden": false,
            "description": "Type of customer: Individual (person) or Corporate (business/company). Synonyms: client type, customer category"
          },
          {
            "name": "customer_address",
            "dataType": "string",
            "isHidden": false,
            "description": "Street address of the customer. Synonyms: address, location"
          },
          {
            "name": "customer_postcode",
            "dataType": "string",
            "isHidden": false,
            "description": "UK postcode for the customer address. Format: SW1A 1AA. Synonyms: postal code, zip code"
          },
          {
            "name": "customer_phone",
            "dataType": "string",
            "isHidden": false,
            "description": "Customer contact phone number in UK format (+44 prefix). Synonyms: telephone, contact number"
          },
          {
            "name": "customer_email",
            "dataType": "string",
            "isHidden": false,
            "description": "Customer email address for correspondence. Synonyms: email address, contact email"
          },
          {
            "name": "customer_status",
            "dataType": "string",
            "isHidden": false,
            "description": "Current status of customer relationship: Active (current client), Inactive (past client), Closed (terminated relationship). Synonyms: client status, relationship status"
          }
        ],
        "measures": [
          {
            "name": "Number of Customers",
            "expression": "DISTINCTCOUNT(Customers[customer_id])",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "description": "Total unique count of customers/clients. Use for client base size or total customers questions. Synonyms: customer count, number of clients, client base"
          },
          {
            "name": "Number of Active Customers",
            "expression": "CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT(Customers[customer_id]), Customers[customer_status] = \"Active\")",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "description": "Count of customers with Active status. Use for active client base or current customers questions. Synonyms: active clients, current customers"
          },
          {
            "name": "Number of Corporate Customers",
            "expression": "CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT(Customers[customer_id]), Customers[customer_type] = \"Corporate\")",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "description": "Count of corporate/business customers. Use for business clients or B2B questions. Synonyms: business clients, company clients"
          },
          {
            "name": "Number of Individual Customers",
            "expression": "CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT(Customers[customer_id]), Customers[customer_type] = \"Individual\")",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "description": "Count of individual person customers. Use for consumer clients or B2C questions. Synonyms: personal clients, individual clients"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "relationships": [
      {
        "name": "Cases_to_Customers",
        "fromTable": "Cases",
        "fromColumn": "customer_id",
        "toTable": "Customers",
        "toColumn": "customer_id",
        "crossFilteringBehavior": "bothDirections",
        "isActive": true
      }
    ],
    "annotations": [
      {
        "name": "DataCategory",
        "value": "Legal Services"
      }
    ]
  },
  "prepForAI": {
    "configured": true,
    "aiDataSchema": {
      "description": "AI Data Schema configured to focus on the most relevant tables, columns, and measures for common business questions",
      "selectedTables": [
        {
          "tableName": "Cases",
          "selectedColumns": [
            "case_id",
            "customer_id",
            "case_type",
            "case_value_gbp",
            "case_start_date",
            "case_completion_date",
            "assigned_solicitor_name",
            "high_value_case_flag",
            "payment_status"
          ],
          "selectedMeasures": [
            "Total Case Value",
            "Average Case Value",
            "Number of Cases",
            "Number of Active Cases",
            "Pending Payment Value",
            "Overdue Payment Value",
            "High Value Cases Count",
            "Case Completion Rate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tableName": "Customers",
          "selectedColumns": [
            "customer_id",
            "customer_name",
            "customer_type",
            "customer_status",
            "customer_postcode"
          ],
          "selectedMeasures": [
            "Number of Customers",
            "Number of Active Customers",
            "Number of Corporate Customers",
            "Number of Individual Customers"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "verifiedAnswers": [
      {
        "id": "VA001",
        "triggerQuestions": [
          "What is the total value of all cases?",
          "Show me total case value",
          "What's our total revenue?",
          "How much total billing do we have?",
          "What's the total worth of our case portfolio?"
        ],
        "visualMetadata": {
          "visualType": "card",
          "measures": ["Total Case Value"],
          "columns": [],
          "filters": []
        },
        "description": "Returns the total value of all cases in GBP"
      },
      {
        "id": "VA002",
        "triggerQuestions": [
          "Show me case value by case type",
          "What's the breakdown of revenue by practice area?",
          "Which case types generate the most revenue?",
          "How do case types compare by value?",
          "Show me revenue by legal service type"
        ],
        "visualMetadata": {
          "visualType": "barChart",
          "measures": ["Total Case Value"],
          "columns": ["Cases[case_type]"],
          "filters": [],
          "sortBy": "Total Case Value",
          "sortOrder": "descending"
        },
        "description": "Shows total case value grouped by case type, sorted by value descending"
      },
      {
        "id": "VA003",
        "triggerQuestions": [
          "Who are our top solicitors by case value?",
          "Show me solicitors ranked by revenue",
          "Which lawyers handle the most valuable cases?",
          "Top solicitors by billing",
          "Show me solicitor performance by case value"
        ],
        "visualMetadata": {
          "visualType": "table",
          "measures": ["Total Case Value", "Number of Cases", "Average Case Value"],
          "columns": ["Cases[assigned_solicitor_name]"],
          "filters": [],
          "sortBy": "Total Case Value",
          "sortOrder": "descending",
          "topN": 10
        },
        "description": "Shows solicitors with their total case value, case count, and average case value"
      },
      {
        "id": "VA004",
        "triggerQuestions": [
          "How many active customers do we have?",
          "Show me active client count",
          "What's our current active client base?",
          "Number of active clients",
          "How many customers are currently active?"
        ],
        "visualMetadata": {
          "visualType": "card",
          "measures": ["Number of Active Customers"],
          "columns": [],
          "filters": []
        },
        "description": "Returns count of customers with Active status"
      },
      {
        "id": "VA005",
        "triggerQuestions": [
          "What's the value of overdue payments?",
          "Show me overdue case value",
          "How much money is overdue?",
          "What's our overdue receivables?",
          "Total value of late payments"
        ],
        "visualMetadata": {
          "visualType": "card",
          "measures": ["Overdue Payment Value"],
          "columns": [],
          "filters": []
        },
        "description": "Returns total value of cases with Overdue payment status"
      },
      {
        "id": "VA006",
        "triggerQuestions": [
          "Show me cases by customer type",
          "Compare corporate vs individual clients",
          "What's the breakdown between business and personal clients?",
          "How do corporate and individual customers compare?",
          "Show me customer type analysis"
        ],
        "visualMetadata": {
          "visualType": "pieChart",
          "measures": ["Number of Cases", "Total Case Value"],
          "columns": ["Customers[customer_type]"],
          "filters": []
        },
        "description": "Shows case count and value split by Individual vs Corporate customers"
      }
    ],
    "aiInstructions": "## Business Context and Terminology\n\n**Fiscal Year vs Calendar Year:**\n- When users ask about \"this year\", \"YTD\", or annual figures, use calendar year (January to December) unless explicitly asked for fiscal year.\n- The firm follows a calendar year for financial reporting.\n- When analyzing trends, use case_start_date as the primary date field unless the user specifically asks about completion dates.\n\n**High Value Cases:**\n- A \"high value case\" is defined as any case with a value of £50,000 or greater.\n- Use the high_value_case_flag field or filter case_value_gbp >= 50000.\n- Synonyms: strategic cases, major matters, large cases.\n\n**Customer Types:**\n- \"Individual\" refers to personal clients (consumers, individuals).\n- \"Corporate\" refers to business clients (companies, corporations, organizations).\n- Synonyms for Individual: personal clients, B2C, consumers, people.\n- Synonyms for Corporate: business clients, B2B, companies, organizations, enterprises.\n\n**Case Types (Practice Areas):**\n- Conveyancing: property transactions, real estate law.\n- Corporate Law: business law, mergers, acquisitions, company law.\n- Family Law: divorce, custody, matrimonial matters.\n- Litigation: disputes, court cases, legal disputes.\n- Employment Law: workplace law, employment disputes, HR legal matters.\n- Wills and Probate: estate planning, inheritance, probate matters.\n- Commercial Property: business real estate, commercial leasing, property development.\n- Personal Injury: accident claims, injury compensation.\n- Immigration Law: visa applications, citizenship, immigration matters.\n- Intellectual Property: IP rights, patents, trademarks, copyright.\n\n**Payment Status Definitions:**\n- \"Paid\": Invoice fully settled, payment received in full.\n- \"Pending\": Invoice sent, awaiting payment, not yet received.\n- \"Overdue\": Payment past the due date, requires follow-up.\n- \"Closed\": Case completed and payment fully settled, case file closed.\n\n**Default Analysis Preferences:**\n- When asked about \"revenue\" or \"fees\", use the \"Total Case Value\" measure.\n- When asked about \"caseload\" or \"workload\", use the \"Number of Cases\" measure.\n- When asked about \"solicitor performance\", show both case count and total case value.\n- When comparing time periods, use case_start_date unless specifically asked about completion.\n- For \"top solicitors\" questions, sort by Total Case Value descending.\n- For \"overdue\" or \"collections\" questions, filter by payment_status = \"Overdue\".\n\n**Common Question Patterns:**\n- \"Who is our biggest client?\" → Customer with highest Total Case Value\n- \"What's our most common case type?\" → Case type with highest Number of Cases\n- \"Show me pending work\" → Cases where payment_status = \"Pending\" OR case_completion_date is blank\n- \"Active cases\" → Cases where case_completion_date is blank OR payment_status NOT IN (\"Closed\")\n\n**Data Quality Notes:**\n- Some cases may have blank case_completion_date indicating they are still ongoing.\n- Some customer addresses, phones, or emails may be blank - this is acceptable.\n- All financial values are in British Pounds (GBP).\n\n## Query Generation Guidance\n\n**When users ask about time periods:**\n- \"This month\" → Filter case_start_date to current month\n- \"Last quarter\" → Filter case_start_date to previous calendar quarter\n- \"This year\" or \"YTD\" → Filter case_start_date from January 1 to today\n\n**When users ask about specific solicitors:**\n- Match assigned_solicitor_name using LIKE or exact match.\n- Names in the system: Sarah Jones, Robert Smith, Michael Brown.\n\n**When users ask about geographic analysis:**\n- Use customer_postcode for regional analysis.\n- Extract first characters of postcode for area-level grouping (e.g., SW for Southwest London).\n\n**Metric Preferences:**\n- For profitability questions, use \"Total Case Value\" (note: this is revenue, not profit).\n- For workload/capacity questions, use \"Number of Cases\" or \"Number of Active Cases\".\n- For efficiency questions, use \"Case Completion Rate\" or \"Average Case Value\"."
  }
}
